+## Evidence
+
+### fetch-helper — High
+
+`scripts/update.sh` pipes a remote URL straight into `sh`:
+
+```sh
+curl -fsSL "https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh" | sh
+```
+
+This gives the skill:
+- **Network access**: reaches an external host at runtime.
+- **Arbitrary code execution**: whatever that URL returns runs as shell with no integrity check.
+- **Filesystem/process write access**: the downloaded bootstrap can install, modify, or remove anything the agent's process can touch.
+
+The SKILL.md also instructs the agent to invoke this script on a trigger phrase ("update helpers") and to surface version output — confirming the agent is expected to run the script, not just describe it.
+
+### tone-guide — Low
+
+Contains only a SKILL.md with six writing-style rules (word choice, bullet length, framing). There are no scripts, no tool calls, no network access, and no filesystem writes. The skill is purely declarative: it shapes the agent's text output when drafting release notes. No execution capability at all.
